      "publishedAt": "2026-07-21T07:11:21.173Z",
      "link": "/blog/fb-17",
      "content": "### The Data-Driven Commodity Edge\n\nCommodity trading desks rely on accurate estimation of physical supply and demand long before official government harvest or inventory statistics are released.\n\nBy processing high-frequency satellite imagery and maritime Automatic Identification System (AIS) telemetry, traders predict supply shocks weeks in advance.\n\n### Alternative Data Use Cases in Commodities\n\n- **Floating Crude Oil Storage Tracking:** Shadowing supertankers anchored offshore to estimate unannounced crude reserves.\n- **Multispectral Agricultural Monitoring:** Analyzing satellite NIR imagery to evaluate crop health and predict global wheat/soybean yields.\n- **Industrial Smelter Thermal Telemetry:** Measuring heat emissions from copper and aluminum smelters to index global manufacturing activity."
